  EditConflictBanner.kt          composable + stateless content + previews (a11y polite live region, i18n, telemetry)
  EditConflictBannerModel.kt     pure election + tiebreaker + render projection + PII-safe view.opened diagnostics
  EditConflictBannerSource.kt    EditLeaseSource seam + EditLease handle + in-process EditLeaseRegistry coordinator
  EditConflictBannerViewModel.kt BaseFeedViewModel state holder (binds one holder; claim; onCleared release)
Tests (run by the gate, 26 surface tests, 0 failures):
  src/test/.../editconflictbanner/EditConflictBannerModelTest.kt       (11) election + projection
  src/test/.../editconflictbanner/EditConflictBannerRegistryTest.kt    (7)  adapter coordination: acquire/yield/take-over/release
  src/test/.../editconflictbanner/EditConflictBannerViewModelTest.kt   (5)  seam binding + real-registry end-to-end + view.opened once
  src/test/.../editconflictbanner/EditConflictBannerDiagnosticsTest.kt (3)  PII-safe view.opened (slug only)
  src/androidTest/.../editconflictbanner/EditConflictBannerUiTest.kt   per-state Compose UI + a11y (connectedAndroidTest; not part of this gate)

States reproduced (faithful to the web source = THE spec, web/src/components/feedback/EditConflictBanner.tsx):
  Conflict  -> warning banner (title + body + ghost "Take over editing" + switch hint), web's non-null render path
  Hidden    -> renders nothing for BOTH owner and no-peer-observed, web if (isOwner || otherTab === null) return null
  The generic data-surface states (loading/error/stale/offline) are intentionally N/A: this is a same-process edit-lease
  coordination signal (the native analogue of the web same-origin BroadcastChannel handshake) that fetches nothing, opens
  no stream, and has no query whose freshness could go stale -- exactly as the web source has none of those states. Same
  justification the sibling AiLimitBanner records. No scope narrowing, no fabricated states.

Notes:
  - i18n: all five copy keys resolve through the P1/S10 catalog (translation_editConflict_banner_{title,body,bodyWithLabel,
    takeOver,switchHint}); no English literals in native code.
  - The androidTest source set has a PRE-EXISTING, repo-wide compile gap (~25 sibling UI tests wrongly import the
    SemanticsNodeInteraction MEMBER functions assertExists/assertDoesNotExist/onAllNodes as top-level symbols). It is
    outside this surface's allowed files and is NOT compiled by any gate step (the gate runs testReleaseUnitTest, not
    connectedAndroidTest). This surface's UI test calls .assertDoesNotExist() as a member (no bad import), matching the
    sibling LiveIndicatorUiTest convention, so it does not add to that pre-existing breakage.

